    <a href="/accounts/create" class="btn" style="margin-right: 10px;">➕ Open New Account</a>
    <a href="/transfers" class="btn">💸 Wire Transfer Funds</a>
</div>

<hr style="border: 0; border-top: 1px solid #eee; margin: 30px 0;">

<h3>System Vulnerabilities Map</h3>
<p>This legacy core banking application models multiple common flaws found in unhardened Node.js systems:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>SQL Injection (SQLi):</strong> Custom authentication and account lookup endpoints construct string payloads directly.</li>
    <li><strong>Broken Access Control / IDOR:</strong> Query parameters (e.g. <code>?userId=X</code>) and missing ownership verification allow unauthorized enumeration of sensitive user balances and transaction wires.</li>
    <li><strong>Mass Assignment:</strong> Creating accounts allows passing unauthorized extra attributes (like arbitrary opening balances).</li>
    <li><strong>Stored & Reflected XSS:</strong> Output tags (<code>&lt;%- ... %&gt;</code>) are used directly on unvalidated input and database attributes.</li>
    <li><strong>Business Logic Flaws:</strong> Account ledger verification does not prevent negative money transactions, allowing reverse asset siphoning.</li>
</ul>

